{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Transform Your Daily Ritual (Our Story band 7)

  A fork of sections/sh-ritual-steps.liquid. The generic section stays on disk,
  keeps its [data-reveal] entrance, and still ships on other templates. This file
  keeps the class .sh-flow, so the entire resting design — the card grid, the
  hairline that passes behind the number badges, the --sh-flow-n arithmetic — is
  shudhi-home.css §20 reused verbatim. .sh-flow--steps is the motion hook.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TWO CONTRACTS, DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  (a) THE ENTRANCE is the house fails-open pattern: resting state is the finished
      state, and .is-armed is only ever added by a script holding the observer
      that clears it.

  (b) THE SCRUB rests at its ZERO end, which is the one deliberate exception on
      this page. That is safe ONLY because everything it drives is decoration with
      no resting appearance: the gold thread and the six accent rings do not exist
      in the reference at rest, so "not yet drawn" IS the reference.

      THE MOMENT ANYONE ROUTES AN ICON, A LABEL, A NUMBER OR A DESCRIPTION
      THROUGH --sh-k, THAT SAFETY IS GONE and this band becomes exactly the
      blank-band failure the rest of the page was migrated away from. Under
      reduced motion §28 forces --sh-k to 1, so a visitor who asked for less
      motion still sees the finished gold progression rather than none of it.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE PAUSE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Step four is slower than its neighbours, by ~320ms. It is keyed on
  :nth-child(4) — position, not the word "Pause" — because the fourth beat of a
  six-beat ritual is where the design puts the breath, and a merchant who
  reorders the steps is reordering the ritual, not just the labels. No JS timer
  is involved and nothing fights the scroll handler: it is one transition-duration.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-story.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}

<section class="sh sh-flow sh-flow--steps"
         {%- if s.animate %} data-sh-reveal{% endif %}
         style="--sh-flow-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-flow-n:{{ section.blocks.size }};">
  <div class="sh-wrap">
    <div class="sh-flow__grid">

      <div class="sh-flow__intro">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <div class="sh-eyebrow" data-sh-fade style="--i:0">{{ s.eyebrow }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h2 class="sh-flow__title sh-serif" data-sh-fade style="--i:1">{{ s.heading }}</h2>
        {%- if s.button_label != blank -%}
          <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid" href="{{ s.button_link | default: '/pages/the-ritual' }}"
             data-sh-fade style="--i:2">
            {{ s.button_label }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Guarded: with no blocks the CSS would hit repeat(0, …) and the
          connector inset — and the scrub's per-step arithmetic — would divide by
          zero. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%} data-sh-scrub marks the element whose travel through the
            viewport drives --sh-k. It goes on the TRACK rather than the section so
            the progression is measured against the row of cards, not against the
            intro column beside them — on desktop those are very different heights. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sh-flow__track"{% if s.animate and s.scrub %} data-sh-scrub{% endif %}>
          {%- comment -%} A sibling of the list, not a child — <ol> only admits <li>.
              Decorative: the sequence is in the markup, this only draws it. The gold
              fill is its ::after in shudhi-story.css, so the grey hairline underneath
              is untouched and still renders when nothing is scrubbing. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="sh-flow__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>

          {%- comment -%} role="list" restores what the reset takes away: .sh ol is
              list-style:none, which drops list semantics in Safari/VoiceOver — and
              the ordering is the point of this section. {%- endcomment -%}
          <ol class="sh-flow__steps" role="list">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              <li class="sh-flow__step" data-sh-fade style="--i:{{ forloop.index0 }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- comment -%} The accent ring. pathLength="1" normalises the
                    circumference so stroke-dashoffset can be driven straight from the
                    scrub with no measurement.

                    IT MUST STAY ABSOLUTELY POSITIONED (§28 does that). §20 makes
                    .sh-flow__num a `display: grid; place-items: center` box holding one
                    thing — the numeral. An in-flow <svg> would become a second grid
                    item and stack the ring ABOVE the number instead of around it. Out
                    of flow, the numeral is still the only grid item and the badge
                    centres exactly as it always did. The numeral itself is never
                    animated: the number is the one thing in this badge that carries
                    meaning. {%- endcomment -%}
                <span class="sh-flow__num" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="sh-flow__ring" viewBox="0 0 34 34" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="17" cy="17" r="16.2" pathLength="1"/></svg>{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon %}
                <h3 class="sh-flow__label">{{ block.settings.label }}</h3>
                <p class="sh-flow__text">{{ block.settings.description }}</p>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if s.animate -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-story-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Story — Steps",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Transform Your Daily Ritual" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "A simple ritual for body, mind & soul." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Explore the ritual" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button_link", "label": "Button link", "info": "Falls back to /pages/the-ritual when empty." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Motion" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true,
      "info": "Turns off the entrance and the gold thread together. The band still renders in full." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "scrub", "label": "Gold thread follows the scroll", "default": true,
      "info": "Fills the connector and draws each number's ring as the band scrolls past. Always shown complete for anyone who has asked for reduced motion." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#e9e0cf",
      "info": "Also fills the step cards and the number badges, which is what hides the connector line behind them. Keep it a solid, light tone." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "step", "name": "Step", "settings": [
      { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Steps are numbered automatically in the order they appear here. The fourth step is the ritual's pause and animates a little slower than its neighbours." },
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "drop", "options": [
        { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" }, { "value": "bubbles", "label": "Bubbles" },
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body" }, { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" },
        { "value": "shower", "label": "Shower" }, { "value": "heart", "label": "Heart" },
        { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" },
        { "value": "hand", "label": "Hand" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Wet" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "description", "label": "Description", "default": "Wet your skin and the soap gently." }
    ] }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6
}
{% endschema %}
